WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.505
Preparation starts with understanding how
the application is put together.

2
00:00:07.585 --> 00:00:14.913
Identify the major components, entry
points, data stores, service boundaries,

3
00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:17.040
and deployment model.

4
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:23.479
AI can help summarize unfamiliar files,
trace high-level call paths,

5
00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:28.947
or describe what a framework route or
handler appears to do.

6
00:00:29.027 --> 00:00:32.044
Use that help to orient yourself,

7
00:00:32.124 --> 00:00:37.620
but keep the summaries tied to specific
files and functions.

8
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.795
A useful summary tells you where to look
next.

9
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.785
It does not replace inspection.

10
00:00:44.865 --> 00:00:51.008
Security review depends heavily on data
flow and trust boundaries.

11
00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:55.937
Track where input enters the system, how
it is parsed,

12
00:00:56.017 --> 00:01:02.806
where authentication is enforced, how
authorization decisions are made,

13
00:01:02.886 --> 00:01:07.520
and where sensitive data is stored or
transmitted.

14
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:14.821
Pay attention to secrets, dependency
configuration, environment variables,

15
00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:18.349
logging behavior, and feature flags.

16
00:01:18.429 --> 00:01:23.817
Vulnerabilities often live in the gap
between components:

17
00:01:23.897 --> 00:01:29.717
a controller trusts a service, a service
trusts a queue message,

18
00:01:29.797 --> 00:01:34.862
or a background job assumes data was
validated earlier.

19
00:01:34.942 --> 00:01:39.575
When using AI to prepare, provide bounded
context.

20
00:01:39.655 --> 00:01:44.505
Ask it to summarize a file, identify
external inputs,

21
00:01:44.585 --> 00:01:52.452
list security-relevant assumptions, or
explain how a particular data path appears to

22
00:01:52.532 --> 00:01:53.071
work.

23
00:01:53.151 --> 00:01:59.832
Avoid dumping a full repository into a
prompt when a smaller slice will do.

24
00:01:59.912 --> 00:02:06.378
Keep notes about what the AI inferred and
what the code actually proves.

25
00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:13.894
Good preparation gives the reviewer a map:
what matters, where boundaries exist,

26
00:02:13.974 --> 00:02:18.500
and which assumptions need direct
verification.
